{"term":"heroine","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:762342399ebdb51a3e","definition":"A female hero.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["shero","hera"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["anti-heroine","antiheroine","Byronic heroine","heroinely","heroineship","heroinic","heroinism","heroinize","mother heroine","superheroine","tragic heroine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d63aa9a514286b5cc7","definition":"A female lead character.","example":"Miss Phyllis Morgan, as the hapless heroine dressed in the shabbiest of clothes, appears in the midst of a gay and giddy throng; she apostrophises all and sundry there, including the villain, and has a magnificent scene which always brings down the house, and nightly adds to her histrionic laurels.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["shero","hera"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["anti-heroine","antiheroine","Byronic heroine","heroinely","heroineship","heroinic","heroinism","heroinize","mother heroine","superheroine","tragic heroine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d85127a5ec74201065","definition":"Characteristic of a heroine; heroic.","example":"Theoxena to free hir Siſters children and hir owne from the laſciuious embraces of King Phillip, put weapons into their weaker hands, and perſwaded them Vt imminens ludibrium morte effugerent; to reſcue themſelues by Death from imminent diſgrace, wherein ſhe had no ſooner preuailed, but with a heroine reſolution ſhe ſhewed them by hir owne example, that what ſhee had taught them, was eaſie to be done.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["heroinely","heroinic"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, r